From: tyn-patches <tyn-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:16:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: STEINS;GATE 0 CONFIG screen

The S;G0 CONFIG screen (BASIC / TEXT / SOUND / VOICE pages, sliders, the
character voices) is ported from Game.exe like the system menu: the module
0x4524a0..0x454e00 is translated from the Ghidra decompile, instruction
10:13 (0x4858c0) runs it for InstructionSet::SG0, its page is drawn on the
system menu layer (0x4579e0 case 5).

- config.cpp: the settings stay in the original's variables (0x2ee7670..,
  rows of Game.exe 0x5c92e0); they are filled from the engine's settings when
  the screen opens and written back every frame (text / auto speed, skip
  mode, trigger stops skip, TIPS notification, auto quick save, the four
  volumes, voice sync / skip, the character voices). Full screen and the
  resolution show full screen and 1920x1080 and do not change.
- Translation fixes (tools/impacto/sg0): float to int conversions Ghidra
  lost (the pulsing cursor, the slider knob), a page function taken for
  __thiscall, Ghidra's sub pieces / CARRY4 / table pointers (EmuPtr), floats
  passed to undefined4 parameters keep their bits, the mouse held and
  position (0x32fc7a8 / 0x32fc7ec) bridged.
- sg0-pc: the engine options menu is off (Type None), CONFIG as a script
  handled sheet.

Verified on MuMu (Android 15 x86_64 emulator, not a real device), sg0-pc:
the four pages; dragging the BGM slider and switching voice skip change the
engine's settings and are still set when the screen is opened again.

